---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import AIValueCalculator from '../../components/AIValueCalculator.astro';
import data from '../../data/ai-value.json';
import '../../styles/editorial-review.css';
const sources = new Map(data.source_ledger.map(source => [source.id, source]));
const slug = title => title.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/^-|-$/g,'');
---
<BlockLayout title={`${data.editorial.headline} · PointCast`} description={data.editorial.dek} author="PointCast Editorial Desk / Codex" isolated immersive showNetworkStrip={false} jsonLd={null}>
  <main class="ed">
    <header class="mast"><a href="/ai">POINTCAST / AI</a><nav aria-label="AI value navigation"><a href="#calculator">Try the calculator</a><a href="#sources">Dated sources</a><a href="/ues/ai-launch-lab">UES evaluation lab</a></nav></header>
    <header class="hero"><div><p class="kicker">AI / Value / Checked {data.editorial.fact_checked_at}</p><h1>{data.editorial.headline}</h1><p class="dek">{data.editorial.dek}</p></div><aside class="hero-plate"><span>COUNT ACCEPTED WORK</span><strong>VALUE</strong><span>Capacity, list-price equivalents and useful results are different measures.</span></aside></header>
    <nav class="jump" aria-label="Article navigation"><a href="#calculator">Calculator</a><a href="#analysis">Full analysis</a><a href="#claim">Read the chart carefully</a><a href="#examples">Worked examples</a><a href="#plans">Plan snapshot</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
    <AIValueCalculator />
    <section id="analysis"><h2>Measure the work behind the multiple.</h2>{data.editorial.sections.map(section => <article id={slug(section.heading)} class="prose"><h3>{section.heading}</h3>{section.paragraphs.map(paragraph => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}{section.source_ids.length > 0 && <p class="source-ref">{section.source_ids.map(id => <a href={sources.get(id).url}>{sources.get(id).title} ↗ </a>)}</p>}</article>)}</section>
    <section id="claim" class="prose"><details><summary>What the reported 5× chart can establish</summary><p>{data.claim_audit.source_description}. These are reported API-equivalent ceilings, not cash benefits. Exact bar values were transcribed from the supplied screenshot and have not been independently reproduced. The original public research was read by the source researcher; this implementation could not reopen it. No paid dashboard or raw logs were accessed.</p><p><a href={sources.get('S1').url}>Read the original SemiAnalysis methodology ↗</a></p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Reported screenshot values / not calculator defaults</caption><thead><tr><th>Monthly plan price</th><th>Reported OpenAI equivalent</th><th>Reported Anthropic equivalent</th><th>Arithmetic ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.claim_audit.figures.map(row => <tr><td>${row.plan_usd}</td><td>${row.openai_api_equivalent_usd.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>${row.anthropic_api_equivalent_usd.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{row.ratio.toFixed(2)}×</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>The tiny workload percentages were not verified and are not imported. API list prices affect the multiple independently of task quality; nothing here establishes a universal winner or an available credit balance.</p></details></section>
    <section id="examples"><h2>Check the arithmetic with four examples.</h2><div class="grid">{data.calculator.worked_examples.map(example => <article class="card"><p class="meta">{example.status}</p><h3>{example.title}</h3><p>{example.interpretation}</p><details><summary>Exact inputs and expected results</summary><pre>{JSON.stringify({inputs:example.inputs,expected:example.expected},null,2)}</pre></details></article>)}</div></section>
    <section id="plans"><h2>A dated price tag is not a token quota.</h2><p>Snapshot checked October 5, 2026. API rates cannot establish included subscription tasks. Recheck current billing, limits, shared usage, features, taxes and account-specific renewal terms before a purchasing decision.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Published plan price snapshot / USD</caption><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Plan</th><th>Published amount</th><th>Billing basis</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.verified_plan_price_snapshot.map(plan => <tr><td>{plan.provider}</td><td>{plan.plan}</td><td>{'monthly_usd' in plan ? `$${plan.monthly_usd}/month` : `$${plan.upfront_usd} up front; $${plan.monthly_equivalent_usd.toFixed(2)} monthly equivalent`}</td><td>{plan.billing}</td><td><a href={sources.get(plan.source_id).url}>Official plan information ↗</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
    <section id="sources"><h2>Trace a price or policy.</h2><ol class="sources">{data.source_ledger.map(source => <li><a href={source.url}>{source.title} ↗</a><small>{source.publisher} · checked {source.checked_at} · {source.kind}</small><p>{source.supports}</p>{'caveat' in source && <p class="note">{source.caveat}</p>}</li>)}</ol></section>
    <footer>PointCast original sourced analysis. No model test, replicated subscription-meter experiment, provider partnership or guaranteed savings is claimed.</footer>
  </main>
</BlockLayout>
<style>.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}.table-wrap table{min-width:620px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.table-wrap th,.table-wrap td{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa}.table-wrap caption{text-align:left;padding:12px 0;font-size:13px}.ed pre{max-width:100%;overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:12px}.ed summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;padding:12px 0}</style>
